{"born":[{"text":"19c9b7ff90","mother":6,"rewritten":false},{"text":"19c9b7ff90","mother":15,"rewritten":false},{"text":"cc698c7950","mother":13,"rewritten":false},{"text":"74795d0494","mother":1,"rewritten":false},{"text":"cc698c7950","mother":21,"rewritten":false},{"text":"74795d0494","mother":1,"rewritten":false},{"text":"2e44b0c4dc","mother":19,"rewritten":true,"failure":null,"why":"The previous code returned 'leave' for known-harmful fruits but still allowed tasting them if novel was false (which it wasn't for known harmful) or if the logic was flawed. More importantly, it lacked a \"safety threshold\" for novel foods; tasting when hungry is dangerous because the cost of being wrong (poison) is high relative to current energy reserves. By only tasting novel items when hunger is low (<50%), Fagi minimizes the risk of starvation from poisoning. Also, `mostlyHarmful` is defined as `harms > feeds`, which correctly identifies poisonous species after a few bad experiences, ensuring she avoids them permanently rather than re-testing.","ms":8647},{"text":"cc698c7950","mother":13,"rewritten":false},{"text":"74795d0494","mother":1,"rewritten":false},{"text":"19c9b7ff90","mother":22,"rewritten":false},{"text":"cc698c7950","mother":13,"rewritten":false},{"text":"19c9b7ff90","mother":5,"rewritten":false},{"text":"36feb66556","mother":9,"rewritten":true,"failure":null,"why":"It prioritizes survival by eating when starving, avoids known poisons unless desperate, and uses a \"taste first\" strategy for novel or high-hunger scenarios to gather data without risking full consumption of toxic items, while efficiently eating fully safe fruits.","ms":8076},{"text":"74795d0494","mother":1,"rewritten":false},{"text":"cc698c7950","mother":19,"rewritten":false},{"text":"19c9b7ff90","mother":15,"rewritten":false},{"text":"19c9b7ff90","mother":2,"rewritten":false},{"text":"19c9b7ff90","mother":7,"rewritten":false},{"text":"d182b5b22b","mother":4,"rewritten":false},{"text":"cc698c7950","mo